{"title":"2010 AIME I Problems/Problem 6","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><div id=\"toc\" class=\"toc\" role=\"navigation\" aria-labelledby=\"mw-toc-heading\"><input type=\"checkbox\" role=\"button\" id=\"toctogglecheckbox\" class=\"toctogglecheckbox\" style=\"display:none\" /><div class=\"toctitle\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><h2 id=\"mw-toc-heading\">Contents</h2><span class=\"toctogglespan\"><label class=\"toctogglelabel\" for=\"toctogglecheckbox\"></label></span></div>\n<ul>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-1\"><a href=\"#Problem\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">1</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-2\"><a href=\"#Solution\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">2</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution</span></a>\n<ul>\n<li class=\"toclevel-2 tocsection-3\"><a href=\"#Solution_1\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">2.1</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 1</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-2 tocsection-4\"><a href=\"#Solution_2\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">2.2</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 2</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-2 tocsection-5\"><a href=\"#Solution_3\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">2.3</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 3</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-2 tocsection-6\"><a href=\"#Solution_4\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">2.4</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 4</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-2 tocsection-7\"><a href=\"#Solution_5\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">2.5</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 5</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-2 tocsection-8\"><a href=\"#Solution_6\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">2.6</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 6</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-2 tocsection-9\"><a href=\"#Solution_7\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">2.7</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 7</span></a></li>\n</ul>\n</li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-10\"><a href=\"#See_Also\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">3</span> <span class=\"toctext\">See Also</span></a></li>\n</ul>\n</div>\n\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem\">Problem</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2010_AIME_I_Problems/Problem_6&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Problem\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/e/f/6efaaf74e576202fad965134bc49c6a34aac4c30.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$P(x)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"41\" height=\"20\" /> be a <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Quadratic\" class=\"mw-redirect\" title=\"Quadratic\">quadratic</a> polynomial with real coefficients satisfying <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/0/d/10d6c0aa7e49a35104097272594cb4bc89026cce.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x^2 - 2x + 2 \\le P(x) \\le 2x^2 - 4x + 3$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"280\" height=\"21\" /> for all real numbers <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/6/e/26eeb5258ca5099acf8fe96b2a1049c48c89a5e6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"12\" height=\"10\" />, and suppose <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/9/2/a92bdefb15a36cdd4331ba542bbca8403c3a4637.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$P(11) = 181$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"100\" height=\"20\" />. Find <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/e/6/8e6e3b44c34bb3fe7444b9db4a92adb48d11a493.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$P(16)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"44\" height=\"18\" />.\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution\">Solution</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2010_AIME_I_Problems/Problem_6&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Solution\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<h3><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_1\">Solution 1</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2010_AIME_I_Problems/Problem_6&amp;action=edit&amp;section=3\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 1\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h3>\n<center><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/6/4/8642816d5b50f02498e44e455af5a0ae225ce976.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"[asy] import graph; real min = -0.5, max = 2.5; pen dark = linewidth(1);  real P(real x) { return 8*(x-1)^2/5+1; } real Q(real x) { return (x-1)^2+1; } real R(real x) { return 2*(x-1)^2+1; } draw(graph(P,min,max),dark); draw(graph(Q,min,max),linetype(&quot;6 2&quot;)+linewidth(0.7)); draw(graph(R,min,max),linetype(&quot;6 2&quot;)+linewidth(0.7)); dot((1,1)); label(&quot;$P(x)$&quot;,(max,P(max)),E,fontsize(10)); label(&quot;$Q(x)$&quot;,(max,Q(max)),E,fontsize(10)); label(&quot;$R(x)$&quot;,(max,R(max)),E,fontsize(10));   /* axes */ Label f; f.p=fontsize(8); xaxis(-2, 3, Ticks(f, 5, 1)); yaxis(-1, 5, Ticks(f, 6, 1));  [/asy]\" width=\"515\" height=\"668\" /></center>\n<p>Let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/1/4/a14e577b3c1dd5a49d7e83837e9ebdab2e7ba2c4.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$Q(x) = x^2 - 2x + 2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"156\" height=\"21\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/b/b/0bb23801717d8f9f404ed3de4b311dc7086a6c0f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$R(x) = 2x^2 - 4x + 3$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"162\" height=\"19\" />. <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Completing_the_square\" title=\"Completing the square\">Completing the square</a>, we have <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/b/e/7be45ca78549edf50d54a244b6453c4e0a285d3e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$Q(x) = (x-1)^2 + 1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"156\" height=\"19\" />, and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/d/b/edbae4e5fdefee819fd073dc0c9b76ba4fa93b58.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$R(x) = 2(x-1)^2 + 1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"165\" height=\"19\" />, so it follows that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/0/6/10694757f2fb26d2b8c3559cda057fe1780ab84b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$P(x) \\ge Q(x) \\ge 1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"137\" height=\"20\" /> for all <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/6/e/26eeb5258ca5099acf8fe96b2a1049c48c89a5e6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"12\" height=\"10\" /> (by the <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Trivial_Inequality\" title=\"Trivial Inequality\">Trivial Inequality</a>). \n</p><p>Also, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/6/6/066584d144d7a746eedafe17ceff904402ebdf8d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1 = Q(1) \\le P(1) \\le R(1) = 1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"226\" height=\"18\" />, so <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/9/9/19980c8b08aeebec855191394f4188780ba25896.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$P(1) = 1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"69\" height=\"18\" />, and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/b/4/4b4cade9ca8a2c8311fafcf040bc5b15ca507f52.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$P$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" /> obtains its minimum at the point <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/e/7/ae7a465ffe5255961382f5777569608be052b783.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(1,1)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"42\" height=\"20\" />. Then <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/e/f/6efaaf74e576202fad965134bc49c6a34aac4c30.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$P(x)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"41\" height=\"20\" /> must be of the form <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/2/e/52e5313a22094f3473318c2d6d84097a0bc28f0c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$c(x-1)^2 + 1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"101\" height=\"19\" /> for some constant <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/3/7/3372c1cb6d68cf97c2d231acc0b47b95a9ed04cc.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$c$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"10\" height=\"10\" />; substituting <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/9/2/a92bdefb15a36cdd4331ba542bbca8403c3a4637.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$P(11) = 181$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"100\" height=\"20\" /> yields <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/a/7/9a74477a040ffe42ad963f75da0e41c09de17429.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$c = \\frac 95$\" style=\"vertical-align: -12px\" width=\"43\" height=\"37\" />. Finally, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/8/4/e8433646cc5e5916015c1a55f14d7057a9b4ccb9.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$P(16) = \\frac 95 \\cdot (16 - 1)^2 + 1 = \\boxed{406}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -12px\" width=\"262\" height=\"37\" />.\n</p>\n<h3><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_2\">Solution 2</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2010_AIME_I_Problems/Problem_6&amp;action=edit&amp;section=4\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 2\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h3>\n<p>It can be seen that the function <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/e/f/6efaaf74e576202fad965134bc49c6a34aac4c30.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$P(x)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"41\" height=\"20\" /> must be in the form <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/8/6/d861c80df854dd5d0c7ef5a2b3a8d90085184f63.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$P(x) = ax^2 - 2ax + c$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"172\" height=\"19\" /> for some real <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/7/d/c7d457e388298246adb06c587bccd419ea67f7e8.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"10\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/3/7/3372c1cb6d68cf97c2d231acc0b47b95a9ed04cc.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$c$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"10\" height=\"10\" />. This is because the <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Derivative\" title=\"Derivative\">derivative</a> of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/e/f/6efaaf74e576202fad965134bc49c6a34aac4c30.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$P(x)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"41\" height=\"20\" /> is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/b/e/7be66f5896e1212b79926525dba8fd67d5219d22.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2ax - 2a$\" width=\"70\" height=\"12\" />, and a global minimum occurs only at <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/4/3/34310f2f36ed6d724838edb08788ee62acb33386.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x = 1$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"42\" height=\"12\" /> (in addition, because of this derivative, the vertex of any quadratic polynomial occurs at <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/2/5/b250a7d94be19932d73b6f79e32ec07dbb15e390.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{-b}{2a}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -12px\" width=\"24\" height=\"37\" />). Substituting <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/e/7/ae7a465ffe5255961382f5777569608be052b783.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(1,1)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"42\" height=\"20\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/6/6/b665703dc1be18c15e1fb73f50d26fe011b1cf3e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(11, 181)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"66\" height=\"18\" /> we obtain two equations:\n</p>\n<center><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/2/8/1280d75a5502cedf7bcf254923bdcf8b62164e8c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$P(11) = 99a + c = 181$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"179\" height=\"18\" />, and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/3/9/0391d44108cc4deef2a67c6c1ab842904914dd26.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$P(1) = -a + c = 1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"148\" height=\"18\" />.</center>\n<p>Solving, we get <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/0/0/00021d032e7443b53804ff2493597356d2f1dc21.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a = \\frac{9}{5}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -12px\" width=\"45\" height=\"37\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/1/5/e155b458691c0db419afa4fbec06a5c17191d3c6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$c = \\frac{14}{5}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -12px\" width=\"52\" height=\"37\" />, so <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/d/4/1d498863f458d682142f88529654c64a655376a3.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$P(x) = \\frac{9}{5}x^2 - \\frac{18}{5}x + \\frac {14}{5}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -12px\" width=\"191\" height=\"37\" />. Therefore, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/6/4/b64d370101522b231aa4a2219b0fba7f7475a1b0.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$P(16) = \\boxed{406}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"110\" height=\"23\" />.\n</p>\n<h3><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_3\">Solution 3</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2010_AIME_I_Problems/Problem_6&amp;action=edit&amp;section=5\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 3\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h3>\n<p>Let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/d/5/ed53d1ee7ba643be25b8c0221ad724069933dfd9.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$y = x^2 - 2x + 2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"124\" height=\"18\" />; note that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/d/5/dd5e1256930a0fee4e3c51e42492d9813ca240f0.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2y - 1 = 2x^2 - 4x + 3$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"173\" height=\"18\" />. Setting <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/a/d/2ad303c5a2d2ee22d477573071eea0b0559c0b54.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$y = 2y - 1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"82\" height=\"15\" />, we find that equality holds when <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/3/4/234b330118777aba0bee513e3ade547ebd70d845.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$y = 1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"42\" height=\"15\" /> and therefore when <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/f/d/2fd96aff1121748fa2ceaefd8bd16cfcc1e8b89a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x^2 - 2x + 2 = 1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"123\" height=\"16\" />; this is true iff <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/4/3/34310f2f36ed6d724838edb08788ee62acb33386.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x = 1$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"42\" height=\"12\" />, so <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/9/9/19980c8b08aeebec855191394f4188780ba25896.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$P(1) = 1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"69\" height=\"18\" />.\n</p><p>Let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/d/8/9d8cdeafdcb906a6cab86989f49281aff48d63db.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$Q(x) = P(x) - x$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"134\" height=\"18\" />; clearly <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/c/8/7c883be69363ba5d52f57ada1ef962aa7a4ec95d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$Q(1) = 0$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"70\" height=\"18\" />, so we can write <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/1/c/11c2758f70129cd3f01d5c8bf90eb172784849bf.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$Q(x) = (x - 1)Q&#39;(x)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"161\" height=\"18\" />, where <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/2/7/827261955d01e0b91631bb4756c806bfb75a2673.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$Q&#39;(x)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"42\" height=\"18\" /> is some linear function. Plug <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/9/d/d9dfe7c7a0b887097fa2227a230fc915ba2e5477.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$Q(x)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"41\" height=\"20\" /> into the given inequality:\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/b/0/5b07a391262185be8056b5397b3714ba08f63c27.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x^2 - 3x + 2 \\le Q(x) \\le 2x^2 - 5x + 3$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"277\" height=\"19\" />\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/3/6/d36b2b0e280effa416c85a38be42c50029ec1c11.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(x - 1)(x - 2) \\le (x - 1)Q&#39;(x) \\le (x - 1)(2x - 3)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"378\" height=\"18\" />, and thus\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/a/d/0ad3db89e4c33ea0bba07a7637fa41f1cff55bda.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x - 2 \\le Q&#39;(x) \\le 2x - 3$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"184\" height=\"18\" />\n</p><p>For all <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/7/6/3767f0665ea4d5f0e9c58452fc5782b42a8a65a2.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x &gt; 1$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"42\" height=\"12\" />; note that the inequality signs are flipped if <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/f/a/1faf5d41cd05857f8f0cbab1eb5a41bb1a6741f4.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x &lt; 1$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"42\" height=\"12\" />, and that the division is invalid for <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/4/3/34310f2f36ed6d724838edb08788ee62acb33386.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x = 1$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"42\" height=\"12\" />. However,\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/e/b/febe17ded1ed7a3ca3939b582d19458a0d3c45f1.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\lim_{x \\to 1}  x - 2 = \\lim_{x \\to 1}  2x - 3 = -1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -11px\" width=\"224\" height=\"23\" />,\n</p><p>and thus by the <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Sandwich_theorem\" class=\"mw-redirect\" title=\"Sandwich theorem\">sandwich theorem</a> <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/9/d/39dd60a1a5aeeea76fb28b0326866b37be883bde.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\lim_{x \\to 1} Q&#39;(x) = -1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -11px\" width=\"120\" height=\"25\" />; by the definition of a continuous function, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/5/f/d5fc851457e6a56640bb6c5fa4e3b4842b1079f3.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$Q&#39;(1) = -1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"88\" height=\"18\" />. Also, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/7/b/f7bd2901acc88e5a7ec1ca873dbdf52fdc22c4a2.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$Q(11) = 170$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"97\" height=\"18\" />, so <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/0/f/c0f51f61e16998e33b60edad23152f6a030aae98.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$Q&#39;(11) = 170/(11-1) = 17$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"218\" height=\"18\" />; plugging in and solving, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/e/e/fee4d9c578dbc8eb454d3e68e7b1d75f72b8da94.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$Q&#39;(x) = (9/5)(x - 1) - 1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"195\" height=\"18\" />. Thus <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/3/4/d3408b46d4114c3bdea6ca5ad4e17bd4e463b7f7.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$Q(16) = 390$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"97\" height=\"18\" />, and so <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/6/4/b64d370101522b231aa4a2219b0fba7f7475a1b0.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$P(16) = \\boxed{406}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"110\" height=\"23\" />.\n</p>\n<h3><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_4\">Solution 4</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2010_AIME_I_Problems/Problem_6&amp;action=edit&amp;section=6\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 4\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h3>\n<p>Let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/8/d/68d797b56b16aad54555b7fc5e5b1a5577f7a01b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$Q(x) = P(x) - (x^2-2x+2)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"227\" height=\"19\" />, then <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/7/f/17f996c2fc9eccec612791d58cdd789f11671f7d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$0\\le Q(x) \\le (x-1)^2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"158\" height=\"19\" /> (note this is derived from the given inequality chain).  Therefore, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/b/c/bbc847d6227152ce4bfee6996b65fe5e9a0ae7bf.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$0\\le Q(x+1) \\le x^2 \\Rightarrow Q(x+1) = Ax^2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"298\" height=\"19\" /> for some real value A.\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/c/c/6ccd2d515f8318ed104e48b8c134082406ca83ee.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$Q(11) = 10^2A \\Rightarrow P(11)-(11^2-22+2)=100A \\Rightarrow 80=100A \\Rightarrow A=\\frac{4}{5}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -12px\" width=\"573\" height=\"37\" />.\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/0/f/b0f8d6464868e95473a8ccbca59ebac4a5556e76.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$Q(16)=15^2A=180 \\Rightarrow P(16)-(16^2-32+2) = 180 \\Rightarrow P(16)=180+226= \\boxed{406}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"661\" height=\"23\" />\n</p>\n<h3><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_5\">Solution 5</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2010_AIME_I_Problems/Problem_6&amp;action=edit&amp;section=7\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 5\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h3>\n<p>Let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/c/0/1c001492d730e68dd15b4d97fb3a7a46ac8afd7b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$P(x) = ax^2 + bx + c$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"161\" height=\"19\" />. Plugging in <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/4/3/34310f2f36ed6d724838edb08788ee62acb33386.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x = 1$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"42\" height=\"12\" /> to the expressions on both sides of the inequality, we see that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/4/f/14f878bde37fc8bf9773a39732612a04d01c3e92.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a + b + c = 1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"102\" height=\"14\" />. We see from the problem statement that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/0/c/a0cfe67362a0dcd3b665983973a7f62bdea2ab7c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$121a + 11b + c = 181$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"169\" height=\"16\" />. Since we know the vertex of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/e/f/6efaaf74e576202fad965134bc49c6a34aac4c30.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$P(x)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"41\" height=\"20\" /> lies at <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/4/3/34310f2f36ed6d724838edb08788ee62acb33386.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x = 1$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"42\" height=\"12\" />, by symmetry we get <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/7/7/8771830d1bd2b89766b8b4b4718014a5c92ae31a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$81a -9b + c = 181$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"147\" height=\"14\" /> as well. Since we now have three equations, we can solve this trivial system and get our answer of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/0/2/e0278c427fa0ebe4d188365a4744f127486d361b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\boxed{406}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"39\" height=\"23\" />.\n</p>\n<h3><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_6\">Solution 6</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2010_AIME_I_Problems/Problem_6&amp;action=edit&amp;section=8\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 6\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h3>\n<p>Similar to Solution 5, let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/c/0/1c001492d730e68dd15b4d97fb3a7a46ac8afd7b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$P(x) = ax^2 + bx + c$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"161\" height=\"19\" />. Note that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/e/7/ae7a465ffe5255961382f5777569608be052b783.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(1,1)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"42\" height=\"20\" /> is a vertex of the polynomial. Additionally, this means that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/5/c/65c23a735b2555446a1f84baafd3f3f210993c88.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$b = -2a$\" width=\"64\" height=\"12\" /> (since <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/2/5/b250a7d94be19932d73b6f79e32ec07dbb15e390.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{-b}{2a}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -12px\" width=\"24\" height=\"37\" /> is the minimum <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/6/e/26eeb5258ca5099acf8fe96b2a1049c48c89a5e6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"12\" height=\"10\" /> point). Thus, we have <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/8/6/d861c80df854dd5d0c7ef5a2b3a8d90085184f63.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$P(x) = ax^2 - 2ax + c$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"172\" height=\"19\" />. Therefore <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/0/3/003c76a62b6753ccedffd3c2b5d57a9af1c18c13.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a - 2a + c = 1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"113\" height=\"13\" />. Moreover, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/9/a/79ab79adcdc91293f1cc9123544dd82e026ab5a1.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$99a + c = 181$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"108\" height=\"14\" />. And so our polynomial is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/3/3/5330808b0097397c1b39dcb8ef5da7d47fe77335.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{9}{5}x^2 - \\frac{18}{5}x + \\frac{14}{5}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -12px\" width=\"128\" height=\"37\" />. Plug in <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/2/c/d2cae13a8f6458d5d8c61ba965d0abb4b08da072.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x = 16$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"52\" height=\"13\" /> to get <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/0/2/e0278c427fa0ebe4d188365a4744f127486d361b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\boxed{406}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"39\" height=\"23\" />.\n</p>\n<h3><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_7\">Solution 7</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2010_AIME_I_Problems/Problem_6&amp;action=edit&amp;section=9\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 7\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h3>\n<p>Very similar to Solution 6, start by noticing that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/e/f/6efaaf74e576202fad965134bc49c6a34aac4c30.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$P(x)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"41\" height=\"20\" /> is between two polynomials, we try to set them equal to find a point where the two polynomials intersect, meaning that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/e/f/6efaaf74e576202fad965134bc49c6a34aac4c30.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$P(x)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"41\" height=\"20\" /> would also have to intersect that point (it must be between the two graphs). Setting <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/3/1/b31ca65ccf9a279c01848309d3fa9516a17ce8d4.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x^2 - 2x + 2 = 2x^2 - 4x + 3$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"217\" height=\"18\" />, we find that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/4/3/34310f2f36ed6d724838edb08788ee62acb33386.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x = 1$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"42\" height=\"12\" />. Note that both of these graphs have the same vertex (at <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/4/3/34310f2f36ed6d724838edb08788ee62acb33386.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x = 1$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"42\" height=\"12\" />), and so <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/e/f/6efaaf74e576202fad965134bc49c6a34aac4c30.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$P(x)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"41\" height=\"20\" /> must also have the same vertex <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/1/f/31fa6b94e5a84b15c9a080cd52edc749580d90c4.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(1, 1)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"38\" height=\"18\" />. Setting <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/2/1/9210f7956e5cc3b8aa5d9f656f6d31123ecd9a4f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$P(x) = ax^2 - 2ax + a + 1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"207\" height=\"21\" /> (this is where we have a vertex at <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/1/f/31fa6b94e5a84b15c9a080cd52edc749580d90c4.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(1, 1)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"38\" height=\"18\" />), we plug in <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/6/8/c6878713578626763c38433b3f4c8c2205ad0c15.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$11$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" /> and find that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/e/2/2e2de9734f2d5d0bcb854f9f8b3a477150beb15d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a = 1.8$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"59\" height=\"14\" />. Evaluating <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/4/4/7443f3cf0c753248bd807201f162021f0543ac1f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1.8x^2 - 3.6x + 2.8$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"144\" height=\"18\" /> when <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/2/c/d2cae13a8f6458d5d8c61ba965d0abb4b08da072.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x = 16$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"52\" height=\"13\" /> (our intended goal), we find that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/6/4/b64d370101522b231aa4a2219b0fba7f7475a1b0.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$P(16) = \\boxed{406}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"110\" height=\"23\" />.\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"See_Also\">See Also</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2010_AIME_I_Problems/Problem_6&amp;action=edit&amp;section=10\" title=\"Edit section: See Also\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<table class=\"wikitable\" style=\"margin:0.5em auto; font-size:95%; border:1px solid black; width:80%;\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td style=\"background:#ccf;text-align:center;\" colspan=\"3\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2010_AIME_I\" title=\"2010 AIME I\">2010 AIME I</a></b> (<b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2010_AIME_I_Problems\" title=\"2010 AIME I Problems\">Problems</a></b> • <b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2010_AIME_I_Answer_Key\" title=\"2010 AIME I Answer Key\">Answer Key</a></b> • <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"http://www.artofproblemsolving.com/Forum/resources.php?c=182&amp;cid=45&amp;year=2010\">Resources</a>)\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Preceded&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2010_AIME_I_Problems/Problem_5\" title=\"2010 AIME I Problems/Problem 5\">Problem 5</a></b>\n</td>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Followed&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2010_AIME_I_Problems/Problem_7\" title=\"2010 AIME I Problems/Problem 7\">Problem 7</a></b>\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td colspan=\"3\" style=\"text-align:center;\"><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2010_AIME_I_Problems/Problem_1\" title=\"2010 AIME I Problems/Problem 1\">1</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2010_AIME_I_Problems/Problem_2\" title=\"2010 AIME I Problems/Problem 2\">2</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2010_AIME_I_Problems/Problem_3\" title=\"2010 AIME I Problems/Problem 3\">3</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2010_AIME_I_Problems/Problem_4\" title=\"2010 AIME I Problems/Problem 4\">4</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2010_AIME_I_Problems/Problem_5\" title=\"2010 AIME I Problems/Problem 5\">5</a> <b>•</b> <a class=\"mw-selflink selflink\">6</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2010_AIME_I_Problems/Problem_7\" title=\"2010 AIME I Problems/Problem 7\">7</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2010_AIME_I_Problems/Problem_8\" title=\"2010 AIME I Problems/Problem 8\">8</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2010_AIME_I_Problems/Problem_9\" title=\"2010 AIME I Problems/Problem 9\">9</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2010_AIME_I_Problems/Problem_10\" title=\"2010 AIME I Problems/Problem 10\">10</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2010_AIME_I_Problems/Problem_11\" title=\"2010 AIME I Problems/Problem 11\">11</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2010_AIME_I_Problems/Problem_12\" title=\"2010 AIME I Problems/Problem 12\">12</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2010_AIME_I_Problems/Problem_13\" title=\"2010 AIME I Problems/Problem 13\">13</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2010_AIME_I_Problems/Problem_14\" title=\"2010 AIME I Problems/Problem 14\">14</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2010_AIME_I_Problems/Problem_15\" title=\"2010 AIME I Problems/Problem 15\">15</a>\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td align=\"center\" colspan=\"3\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=AIME_Problems_and_Solutions\" title=\"AIME Problems and Solutions\"> All AIME Problems and Solutions</a></b>\n</td></tr></tbody></table>\n<div class=\"print\">\n<div style=\"display:flex;width:100%;justify-content:space-between;align-items:center\">\n<div>\n<p><span class=\"mw-default-size\" typeof=\"mw:File\"><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=File:AMC_Logo.png\" class=\"mw-file-description\"><img src=\"https://artofproblemsolving.com/wiki/images/d/d1/AMC_Logo.png\" decoding=\"async\" width=\"97\" height=\"84\" class=\"mw-file-element\" /></a></span>\n</p>\n</div>\n<div style=\"flex-grow:1;text-align:right\">\n<p>These problems are copyrighted &#169; by the <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"https://www.maa.org\">Mathematical Association of America</a>. \n</p>\n</div>\n<div style=\"clear:both;\"></div>\n</div></div>\n<!-- \nNewPP limit report\nCached time: 20261017222327\nCache expiry: 86400\nReduced expiry: false\nComplications: [show‐toc]\nCPU time usage: 0.055 seconds\nReal time usage: 0.079 seconds\nPreprocessor visited node count: 612/1000000\nPost‐expand include size: 1786/2097152 bytes\nTemplate argument size: 108/2097152 bytes\nHighest expansion depth: 3/100\nExpensive parser function count: 0/100\nUnstrip recursion depth: 0/20\nUnstrip post‐expand size: 19595/5000000 bytes\n-->\n<!--\nTransclusion expansion time report (%,ms,calls,template)\n100.00%   12.261      1 -total\n 58.27%    7.144      1 Template:AIME_box\n 39.26%    4.814      1 Template:MAA_Notice\n-->\n\n<!-- Saved in parser cache with key wiki-wiki_:pcache:8590:|#|:idhash:canonical and timestamp 20261017222327 and revision id 204943. Rendering was triggered because: api-parse\n -->\n</div>"}